			"type": "text",
			"text": "Concavenator was a theropod dinosaur discovered in La Huérguina formation of Spain. Its name means 'Cuenca hunter', Cuenca being the province it was discovered in. It was a rather unique dinosaur about 5 to 6 meter long and weighing 320 to 400 Kilograms, unlike its bigger cousins, this dinosaur’s neural spines grew tall towards the end forming a sail of sorts. The holotype of this animal was also rather complete, giving us a good idea of its looks."
